    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Excellent location, minutes from Famous River Moy this 4-bedroom terraced property offering an excellent refurbishment opportunity within walking distance of Ballina town centre.\n\nThe property requires comprehensive refurbishment and modernisation throughout, providing the purchaser with an ideal opportunity to redesign and upgrade the accommodation to their own specification. Importantly, a new roof has recently been fitted together with new fascia and soffit, while the property also benefits from white PVC windows and a PVC front entrance door.\n\nExternally, there is an small, enclosed garden to the front, while to the rear lies a particularly generous and unusually long garden, offering excellent outdoor space for a property in such a central location. A side lane runs alongside the terrace.\n\nWith an attractive guide price of 115,000, No. 15 Corcoran Terrace should appeal to builders, investors and purchasers seeking a renovation project in a highly convenient Ballina location.\n\nBallina has established an excellent reputation as a tourist and fishing centre nestling between the Ox and Nephin mountains and the world-renowned River Moy. Property is situated on Bunree Road and walking distance 200 meters to River Moy. Approx. 16km to Foxford, 37km to Ireland West Airport Knock and 39km to Castlebar. \n\nAmenities in Ballina include primary and secondary schools, churches, hotels, supermarkets, train station, bus station, traditional pubs, restaurants as well as B&B's and Guesthouses. \n\nFEATURES:\nPrime town-centre location\nNew roof, fascia & soffit\nExcellent refurbishment opportunity\nElectricity connected\nClose proximity to Famous River Moy\nLarge rear garden with rear lane access\nAttractive guide price of 115,000\nQualifies for vacant home grant 50,000\n\n"
      },
